I have a very preliminary set of nethack information available on 
the world-wide-web.

The WWW is a global hypermedia network sitting on top of the internet,
which incorporates most of the common protocols including ftp, wais,
gopher, archie, etc.  See comp.infosystems.www for more info.

My sub-web on nethack is *very* preliminary; in fact there's more 
missing than present, and dangling pointers abound.  I'm making this
announcement this early in hopes of soliciting volunteers to help
put the information together.

The URL http://info.cern.ch/roeber/Nethack/objects/objects.html is
probably the best place to start.  Only the "Amulets" category is
finished, I'm partway though "Potions."  All the concepts, 
strategies, etc. are yet to be done, but you can see what's planned.

Eventually there will be an introductory page, with pointers to
other information too, including the r.g.h FAQ, the Wheaton spoilers,
the source archive, etc.

I'm mostly limited now by typing speed and spare time availability.
Anybody who wishes to contribute is very welcome.

